Theory navigation ▾ Canon 10 · Inverse Resonance Ladder Equation 10 A pattern may point backward toward causes, but it does not name them by itself. Equation 10 defines a disciplined inverse path from observed pattern to ranked possible causes. It preserves direct witness, generates alternatives, tests ordinary explanations first, applies controls, and only increases confidence when repeated evidence survives comparison. Open the Equation Climb the Ladder Use the Protocol Back to Canon Πν⁻¹ Move backward carefully: observation first, alternatives second, cause last. Watch · The Explainer A pattern may point backward toward causes, but it does not name them by itself. A short spoken tour of Equation 10: the disciplined path from an observed pattern to ranked possible causes — ordinary explanations first, confidence increased only under test. Press play and let the page explain itself. Your browser does not support the video element. The same tour is written out across this page. Canon Identity Equation record. Number Equation 10 Canonical title Inverse Resonance Ladder Primary symbol \( \Pi_{
